<header class="page-header">
  <h1>Import Xero exports by file</h1>
  <%= link_to "← Settings", settings_path, class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
</header>

<div class="notice notice-info">
  <p>The usual way in is <%= link_to "the Xero connection under Settings", xero_connection_path %>, which pulls everything over the API. These uploads are the fallback: Xero's CSV exports, one at a time, in order. Every importer is idempotent, so re-running updates rather than duplicates.</p>
</div>

<div class="kpi-grid">
  <% @importers.each_with_index do |imp, i| %>
    <article class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label"><%= i + 1 %>. <%= imp[:name] %></div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 12px;font-size:13px;">
        <% if imp[:run_before] %>
          ✓ imported (upload again to update)
        <% else %>
          not run yet
        <% end %>
      </p>
      <%= link_to "Upload CSV →", imp[:path], class: "btn btn-primary" %>
    </article>
  <% end %>
</div>
